  m_Name: Northern Giant Hornet
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  bugName: 'Northern Giant Hornet '
  info: "The Northern Giant Hornet are native to temperate regions in China, Korea,
    Japan, and India. \n\nTheir size ranges from 3.5 to 5cm in length. They are the
    largest species of hornet in the world. These hornets were first spotted in Canada
    on August 2019 on Vancouver Island. \n\nThey pose an ecological threat due to
    their consumption of butterflies, beetles, dragonflies, and many others"
